# JSON is checked out with LF on every platform.
#
# Why this file exists: `page_blob_fixture.json` is compared **byte for byte**
# against what the page codec emits, and the codec emits `\n`. With no
# .gitattributes, a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true, the GitHub runner
# default) rewrites the fixture to CRLF and the comparison fails at offset 2
# with `'{\n'` vs `'{\r\n'` — on Windows only, invisibly to anyone developing
# on macOS or Linux.
#
# The failure message helpfully suggests CENTROIDX_REGEN_FIXTURES=1. On Windows
# that is a trap: regenerating there writes CRLF into the fixture and breaks
# macOS and Linux instead. Pinning the checkout is the fix; regenerating is not.
*.json eol=lf
